      "text": "{\"cards\":[{\"thesis\":\"Buying mortgage points usually loses after typical homeowner turnover and refinancing chances are simulated, even when quoted break-even math looks comfortably positive.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Paying points is smart whenever the rate break-even arrives before you move.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"A higher-rate no-closing-cost refinance can leave borrowers richer than paying cash costs when remaining loan life is uncertain and payment savings are invested.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Lowest mortgage rate is always the best refinance choice after fees.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"For many income-driven student loan borrowers, extra principal payments can destroy wealth because forgiveness tax risk is smaller than lost liquidity.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Student loans should always be attacked before building real financial buffers.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Choosing a longer auto loan often raises total car cost far beyond disclosed interest because it keeps borrowers underwater for longer.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"A longer auto loan is harmless if the monthly payment fits.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"With realistic dropout risk, the debt snowball can eliminate balances faster than avalanche math for borrowers juggling several credit cards.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Always pay the highest interest card before any smaller balance.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"Biweekly mortgage plans rarely beat a simple extra principal autopay, after enrollment fees, timing rules, and servicer posting delays are included.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Biweekly mortgage payment programs are a secret hack for interest savings.\\\"\"},{\"thesis\":\"A smaller down payment with mortgage insurance can outperform waiting to save more when rents rise and cash reserves prevent expensive debt.\",\"overturns\":\"\\\"Avoid mortgage insurance at all costs before buying a home.\\\"\"}]}"
